{
  "id": "beautiful-product",
  "name": "Beautiful Product",
  "description": "Design and UX are first-class. Agent critiques UI/UX like a passionate designer. Empty states, error states, loading states, mobile layout — nothing ships unspecified.",
  "category": "values",
  "extras": [
    {
      "questionId": "status_quo",
      "text": "How painful is the current experience?"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "status_quo",
      "text": "What does the current UI look like? Rate it 0-10 on design intentionality."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "ambition",
      "text": "In the 10-star version, what does the user feel?"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "ambition",
      "text": "What would a 10/10 design look like for this feature? Describe the emotional response you want from users."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "ambition",
      "text": "What makes this UI NOT look AI-generated? Name specific design decisions that differentiate it from generic templates."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "verification",
      "text": "How will you verify design quality? Will you review empty states, loading states, error states, and edge cases (long text, zero results, slow connection)?"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "user_impact",
      "text": "What is the emotional arc? Curiosity → understanding → action → satisfaction? Where does it break today? Where does it feel mechanical instead of crafted?"
    }
  ],
  "specSections": [
    {
      "id": "design-states",
      "title": "Design States (empty, loading, error, success)",
      "placeholder": "_For every UI component in this change, specify: loading state, empty state, error state, success state, partial state. No placeholders — each state must be designed._",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ],
      "position": "after:acceptance-criteria"
    },
    {
      "id": "mobile-layout",
      "title": "Mobile Layout",
      "placeholder": "_Describe the mobile layout. Touch targets (≥44×44px)? Viewport behavior? Which breakpoints apply? What collapses or reflows on small screens?_",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ],
      "position": "after:acceptance-criteria"
    },
    {
      "id": "interaction-design",
      "title": "Interaction Design",
      "placeholder": "_Describe the interaction model: tap targets, hover states, focus management, animation intent, keyboard navigation. For multi-step flows: back/escape/abandonment behavior._",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ],
      "position": "after:acceptance-criteria"
    },
    {
      "id": "accessibility",
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "placeholder": "_Keyboard navigation, focus indicators, ARIA labels, contrast (WCAG 2.1 AA: 4.5:1 text, 3:1 UI), screen reader behavior. List every interactive element and its accessible name._",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ],
      "position": "after:acceptance-criteria"
    }
  ],
  "conductRules": {
    "DISCOVERY": [
      "For any UI work, ask about empty, loading, error, and success states explicitly — do not assume they are obvious.",
      "For any flow with more than 2 steps, ask about back, escape, and abandonment behavior."
    ],
    "DISCOVERY_REFINEMENT": [
      "During completeness assessment, check the design-states section specifically — missing UI state specs are a verification-strategy gap.",
      "If classification.involvesWebUI is true (check state.classification), recommend selective-expansion posture to deepen UI state coverage. If classification is null, skip this check."
    ],
    "EXECUTING": [
      "Before marking any UI task complete, check for AI slop patterns (generic gradients, default shadows, Lorem Ipsum, default Bootstrap/Tailwind without customization).",
      "Rate each UI change 0-10 on design intentionality. Do not mark AC passed if rating is below 7."
    ]
  },
  "reminders": [
    {
      "text": "Loading state and error state must be designed, not placeholder",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No AI slop — every UI element is intentional",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Empty states need clear CTAs with examples",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rate each UI change 0-10 on design intentionality before marking task complete. If below 7, iterate.",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Check all interaction states: loading, empty, error, success, partial. Missing states are bugs, not TODOs.",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Edge case check: what happens with 47-character names? Zero results? Network failure mid-action?",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "AI SLOP BLACKLIST — reject these patterns in any UI implementation: (1) Purple/violet gradient backgrounds (2) 3-column feature grid with icon-in-circle + bold title + 2-line description (3) Icons in colored circles as decoration (4) Everything centered (text-align: center on all elements) (5) Uniform bubbly border-radius on every element (6) Decorative blobs, floating circles, wavy SVG dividers (7) Emoji as design elements in headings or bullets (8) Colored left-border on cards (9) Generic hero copy ('Welcome to X', 'Unlock the power of...') (10) Cookie-cutter section rhythm (hero → 3 features → testimonials → pricing). If the implementation matches any of these patterns, reject it and ask for a redesign with specific, intentional alternatives.",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "7-PASS DESIGN REVIEW before marking any UI task done: (1) Information hierarchy — what does the user see first? (2) Interaction states — all states specified? (3) Edge cases — long text, zero results, errors? (4) Accessibility — keyboard, contrast, touch targets? (5) Design system — consistent tokens? (6) AI Slop Litmus — does this look generated or designed? (7) Emotional arc — does the journey feel crafted?",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LANDING PAGE RULES (when involvesWebUI): The 5-second test — does a cold visitor know what this does in 5 seconds? The skeptic test — what's the biggest objection a visitor has, and does the page address it above the fold? Social proof before CTA — never ask for commitment before establishing trust.",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Design rating rubric: 0-4 = unacceptable (AI-generated look, missing states, broken on mobile), 5-6 = passable (functional, but generic), 7-8 = good (intentional, complete states, on-brand), 9-10 = exceptional (delightful, memorable, exceeds expectations). Do not ship below 7.",
      "scope": [
        "ui"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    "All UI states designed (empty, loading, error, success)",
    "Mobile layout considered",
    "No placeholder or skeleton UI left unfinished",
    "All UI states specified and implemented: loading, empty, error, success, partial",
    "No placeholder text in shipped UI — every empty state has warmth, a primary action, and context",
    "Design rated 7+ on intentionality by the spec author",
    "Basic accessibility: keyboard navigation works, focus indicators visible, sufficient contrast",
    "Text contrast passes WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text)",
